<h1>Add your modules</h1>

<p>It's pretty simple to add yourself to the list of CPAN authors on our front
page. Repository links can point to GitHub, GitLab, Bitbucket, or another web
host. The supported CI and coverage badges currently use GitHub repositories;
CPAN version and CPANTS badges remain available for other hosts.</p>

<p>You can add your registration using GitHub's web editor. CI services are
optional; CPAN version and CPANTS badges are available without them.</p>
<p>Register your own CPAN account. If you are helping another author, send them
the prepared JSON and these instructions so they can submit their registration.</p>

<h2>Prepare your registration</h2>
<form id="registration-form">
  <div class="mb-3">
    <label for="registration-cpan">CPAN author ID</label>
    <input id="registration-cpan" class="form-control" required pattern="[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]*" autocomplete="off">
  </div>
  <div class="mb-3">
    <label for="registration-github">GitHub username (optional)</label>
    <input id="registration-github" class="form-control" autocomplete="off">
  </div>
  <fieldset class="mb-3">
    <legend>Services you already use</legend>
    <label><input id="registration-actions" type="checkbox"> GitHub Actions</label>
    <label><input id="registration-coveralls" type="checkbox"> Coveralls</label>
    <label><input id="registration-codecov" type="checkbox"> Codecov</label>
    <label><input id="registration-cirrus" type="checkbox"> Cirrus CI</label>
  </fieldset>
  <div class="mb-3">
    <label for="registration-workflows">GitHub Actions workflow names (one per line)</label>
    <textarea id="registration-workflows" class="form-control" rows="2" placeholder="CI"></textarea>
  </div>
  <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Generate JSON</button>
  <p id="registration-error" role="alert"></p>
</form>
<div id="registration-result" hidden>
  <p>Create <code id="registration-filename"></code> in the <code>authors</code> directory,
  and paste this JSON into the file:</p>
  <label for="registration-json">Registration JSON</label>
  <textarea id="registration-json" class="form-control" rows="18" readonly></textarea>
</div>
<script src="/js/onboarding.js" defer></script>

<h2>Submit your registration</h2>
<ol>
<li>Sign in to GitHub and open the
<a href="https://github.com/PerlToolsTeam/dashboard/new/master/authors">new-file editor in the authors directory</a>.</li>
<li>Name the file <code>YOURCPANID.json</code> and paste the generated JSON. With JavaScript
 disabled, copy <a href="https://github.com/PerlToolsTeam/dashboard/blob/master/authors/DAVECROSS.json">an existing registration</a>
 and change its author ID, GitHub username, and service settings.</li>
<li>Commit the file and follow GitHub's prompts to propose a pull request. GitHub
can create the fork for you, as described in its
<a href="https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/working-with-files/managing-files/creating-new-files">new-file instructions</a>.</li>
<li>After the pull request is merged, the next site refresh gathers your release
metadata and adds your dashboard.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Supported CI services</h2>

<p>We currently support the following CI services:</p>

<div id="accordion">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-header" id="headingOne">
      <h3 class="mb-0">
        <button class="btn btn-link" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#collapseOne"
                aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="collapseOne">
          Github Actions
        </button>
      </h3>
    </div>
    <div id="collapseOne" class="collapse show" aria-labelledby="headingOne" data-parent="#accordion">
      <div class="card-body">
        <p>Github Actions can do many things. But we're just using it to run tests on each commit
          and report on the success or failure of the test run. Add a directory called
          <tt>.github/workflows</tt> to your code repository and in that directory create a YAML
          file that runs the processes that you want to run. A basic workflow file for testing a
          CPAN module might look
          <a href="https://github.com/davorg/array-compare/blob/master/.github/workflows/perltest.yml">something like this</a>.</p>
        <p>You can track as many Github Actions as you like and the badges will stack on top of
          each other in your dashboard (this isn't currently as pretty as I'd like it, but we're
          working on it). Remember the values of the <tt>name</tt> keys in your YAML files as you'll
          need to add those to the <tt>ci.gh_workflow_names</tt> option in your new configuration
          file. Alternatively, list YAML filenames such as <tt>test.yml</tt> in
          <tt>ci.gh_workflow_files</tt>.</p>
        <p>Distributions inherit your author-level settings. To change one distribution,
          add a <tt>distribution_ci</tt> object keyed by its distribution name. For example:</p>
        <pre>{
  "distribution_ci": {
    "Example-Dist": {
      "gh_workflow_names": [],
      "gh_workflow_files": ["test.yml"],
      "use_coveralls": 0
    }
  }
}</pre>
        <p>Only fields you supply override the author defaults. Set
          <tt>use_gh_actions</tt> to 0 for a distribution without workflows.
          Cached builds apply these settings without refreshing release metadata.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-header" id="headingThree">
      <h3 class="mb-0">
        <button class="btn btn-link" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#collapseThree"
                aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="collapseThree">
          Coveralls.io
        </button>
      </h3>
    </div>
    <div id="collapseThree" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="headingThree" data-parent="#accordion">
      <div class="card-body">
        <p><a href="https://coveralls.io/">Coveralls.io</a> measures your test coverage.  Log in
          with your Github credentials and turn on the repos that you want to use. You also have to
          find a way to feed coverage data to your Coveralls.io account. For example, using GitHub
          Actions, I define a job like this:
        <pre>
  coverage:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    container: davorg/perl-coveralls:latest
    name: Test coverage
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - name: Install modules
        run: cpanm -n --installdeps .
      - name: Coverage
        env:
          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
        run: cover -test -report Coveralls
        </pre>
        <p>Next time you commit something to one of your repos, you will also get coverage
          information appearing at Coveralls.io.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-header" id="headingFive">
      <h3 class="mb-0">
        <button class="btn btn-link" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#collapseFive"
                aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="collapseFive">
          Codecov.io
        </button>
      </h3>
    </div>

    <div id="collapseFive" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="headingFive" data-parent="#accordion">
      <div class="card-body">
        <p>We support <a href="https://codecov.io/">Codecov.io</a>, but haven't written instructions
          for it yet.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-header" id="headingSix">
      <h3 class="mb-0">
        <button class="btn btn-link" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#collapseSix"
                aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="collapseSix">
          Cirrus CI
        </button>
      </h3>
    </div>

    <div id="collapseSix" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="headingSix" data-parent="#accordion">
      <div class="card-body">
        <p>We support <a href="https://cirrus-ci.org/">Cirrus CI</a>, but haven't written instructions
          for it yet.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-header" id="headingSeven">
      <h3 class="mb-0">
        <button class="btn btn-link" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#collapseSeven"
                aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="collapseSeven">
          AppVeyor
        </button>
      </h3>
    </div>

    <div id="collapseSeven" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="headingSeven" data-parent="#accordion">
      <div class="card-body">
        <p>We support <a href="https://appveyor.com/">AppVeyor</a>, but haven't written instructions
          for it yet.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>Fixing issues</h2>

A number of issue that could be discovered by the CPAN Dashboard and how to fix them.

<ul>
<li>Add a link to the code repos to the metadata of all of your CPAN modules.
(Gabor has <a href="https://perlmaven.com/how-to-add-link-to-version-control-system-of-a-cpan-distributions"> a tutorial about that</a>.)</li>
<li>Configure GitHub Actions</li>
<li>Configure Coveralls</li>
<li>...</li>
</ul>

